<p>"If you wait patiently, you will be rewarded with IA."</p> 
<p>This is what you were told when it started.</p>
<p>Now you have IA. Chapters 5 and 6 are available to read <a href="/read/64">here</a>. These are the final chapters of IA IA IA.</p>
<p>It's been half a year since chapter 4. During this time, I battled illness and injury. Shortly after chapter 4 was completed, I came down with a cold that once again turned into bronchitis. A few months later, I learned a new hobby. Skateboarding is tough, isn't it? I fell backwards and bruised my tailbone, which made sitting and working more difficult. Little ducks must wear protective gear. I was, too, but I still got hurt...</p>
<p>Even though it was hard, I did more comics work than ever. By the way, the store is open. That was part of the work.</p>
<p>In other words, IA IA IA will soon be available to buy <a href="/store">here</a>. It's my two years of work, so if you enjoyed it, I hope you'll take a copy home. I actually hate mailing things, but I'll do it for you, so please...!</p>
<p>There are other nice things for you to buy there as well, so come in with an open mind.</p>
<p>IA IA IA is itself new, in a way. The pages have been edited to look nicer. I was using my 2023 process in 2025, but when a friend told me, I had to try something new. I've learned a lot, after all.</p>
<p>In the end, it's complete. When I planned IA IA IA, I wanted it to be like reading a dream. I had a lot of dreams while writing IA IA IA. Dreams that reminded me of who I was, and what I wanted. (Although, one time, I dreamed IA stood for "irate and angry," which isn't what I wanted at all. If you're irate and angry, can't we talk it out?)</p>
<p>One of my dreams for you is to understand IA, so think hard when you read it.</p>
<p>Now that IA is delivered, I'm taking a break. Writing and drawing comics is hard work. I am trying to be aimless for a long time. But once I'm done, there will be comics again. I won't do something like this right away. You will probably see some shorter comics -- please give them the same care you gave to me.</p>
<p>However, there's a great comic idea. I've been researching for it since last year, even though it's still not a done deal. It's possible it will be even longer than IA IA IA, so the release won't be all at once. If you support me, you won't regret it. It has nothing to do with IA IA IA, but it will show an evolution in my ideas. It may appear <a href="/hunters">here</a>.</p>
<p>I may sound different in the future, but I don't know if I can stop using this voice in the end. I'm a little sad, though, so maybe my crying will break the spell.</p>
<p><a href="/read/64">The final chapters of IA IA IA are here.</a></p>
<p><a href="/store">You will soon be able to purchase IA IA IA here.</a></p>
<p>Please enjoy it.</p>